  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "kNet: Fix content length calculation when 4 bytes are used",
  "description": "This uses a varint type which can only have 1, 2, or 4 bytes\nand fits an extra bit into the range at 4 bytes compared to\nother types in exchange for not having a possibility of 3 bytes.\n\nOnly the lower seven bits from the second-to-least significant\nbyte should be used, similar to the least significant byte.\n\nThis removes 1 bit from the range, which also makes overflow of\nan int impossible even after adding two (even though this is\nan inherently unsigned value and could be unsigned), thus addressing\nOSS-Fuzz 493466401.\n\nNone of the example files in #5956 use lengths that would require\nmore than two bytes.\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
